      "content": "thanks. but it feels like \"harm potential\" and \"dehumanizing stereotypes\" are pretty vague terms. if you look at the big players, there's a clear trend where companies are moving towards more aggressive flagging to prevent \"misinformation\" or \"harmful tropes,\" even if the user says it's just a joke. \n\nfrom a policy standpoint, would you say it's becoming the standard to prioritize the prevention of social harm over the protection of satire? like, is the industry consensus shifting to favor safety over free expression in these cases?",
